1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,400
The sensor that made my robot
look at people got discontinued.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,800
So I built the replacement
and tested it on one eye.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,200
This is that test.

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,600
A tiny AI camera sits under the eye
and finds my face.

5
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:17,000
It works out where the face is
and sends that over two wires.

6
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,400
No Pi. No PC. No wifi.

7
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,800
The eye just looks where it is told.

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,200
Blinking and pupil size
are its own business.

9
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:30,600
About $64 of parts.
A second eye is under $12.

10
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:34,200
The robot it was built for
is called IRIS.

11
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:38,500
It is using this right now.
